{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0161","billNumberShort":"S.B. 161","billNumberLong":"SB0161S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1225","shortTitle":"Evaluations in Guardianship Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WEILET","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Weiler, Todd","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"BALLAMG","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Ballard, Melissa G.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to guardianship.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that a person's rights under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 are not altered or abridged by Utah code provisions related to the rights of a person alleged to be incapacitated;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to the qualifications of a health care provider appointed by a court to assess an individual alleged to be incapacitated, and standards for the tools the health care professional uses for the assessment;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that the court appointed health care professional's report must be filed with the court;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies that a court appointed visitor's report must be filed with the court;<hr><ltbullet>provides that the court appointed health care provider may interview the person seeking to be appointed a guardian, but may not base the health care provider's assessment solely or predominately on that individual's opinion; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Amy Shewan","fiscalAnalyst":"Gary R. Syphus","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/23/2026","trackingID":"OFDDHUYIEA","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-19 14:06:22.073","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr